; Pure-OCaml pt2 reader: zip, strided tensor, pickle (no libtorch dependency).

; [opickle] is here for one reason: opickle's own test suite has no js mode, so
; a 32-bit-int regression added there could never be observed. Its Src module is
; re-exported publicly for exactly this ("unit-tested in isolation"), so the
; backend-sensitive assertion lives in this JS-enabled suite instead. The fix
; itself still belongs upstream. See .ai/js_backends_design.md.

(library
 (name pt2_test)
 (modules pt2_test)
 (libraries core err_trace pt2 zipc opickle bytesrw)
 ; See test/native4d/dune for why [js] carries no `enabled_if`.
 (inline_tests
  (modes best js))
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_expect)))

; ATen bridge coverage stays separate from [pt2_test], which is deliberately
